@startuml transmitter_states
title Transmitter: Phase state machine (python-statemachine)
skinparam shadowing false
hide empty description

[*] --> IDLE

IDLE : Sends a frame of silence whenever the\ncontroller queue is below 80 ms.\nKeeps the broadcast alive between streams.
BUFFERING : Sends nothing.\nWaits for the prebuffer (Audio buffer option).\nAlso where a stream ends up when its audio runs dry,\nso receivers conceal the gap instead of decoding silence.
PLAYING : Sends one frame of audio, with volume and\nmute applied, whenever the controller queue\nis below 80 ms.

IDLE --> BUFFERING : begin\n(feed(): first audio of a stream)
BUFFERING --> PLAYING : ready\n(buffered audio reaches the prebuffer)
PLAYING --> BUFFERING : starve\n(buffer empty: underrun counted and logged)
BUFFERING --> IDLE : reset\n(clear(): stream ended or seek)
PLAYING --> IDLE : reset\n(clear(): stream ended or seek)

legend bottom
  Events that do not apply in the current state do nothing
  (allow_event_without_transition), so callers can raise
  begin on every chunk and reset whenever a stream ends.
endlegend
@enduml
